Package: DisentFunSpaces
Type: Package
Title: Build and Compare Functional Spaces from Mixed-Type Trait Data
Version: 0.5.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Aurèle", "Toussaint", email = "aurele.toussaint@cnrs.fr",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Pablo", "Tedesco", role = "ctb"),
    person("Gaël", "Grenouillet", role = "ctb"),
    person("Liis", "Kasari-Toussaint", role = "ctb"),
    person("Sébastien", "Brosse", role = "ctb"))
Description: Generalises the framework of Toussaint et al. (2026, Ecography,
    <doi:10.1002/ecog.08578>) to any trait dataset. Traits are described by a
    type (continuous, ordinal, nominal, binary, multichoice, fuzzy-coded,
    circular) and assigned to functional dimensions (e.g. locomotion, diet,
    reproduction). A functional space is built for each dimension and for any
    combination of dimensions from a generalised Gower distance (Pavoine et
    al. 2009, <doi:10.1111/j.1600-0706.2008.16668.x>) followed by a Principal
    Coordinates Analysis. Spaces are compared with Procrustes tests, and
    species-level functional uniqueness (FUn), specialisation (FSp) and FUSE
    are computed in each space. Non-native species are positioned relative
    to the native fauna (functional novelty, loss of native uniqueness,
    change in functional richness with null models). A 'shiny' application exposes the full
    workflow. Example data: observed traits of 2000 bird species, described by the traits of
    Toussaint et al. (2026), from AVONET
    (Tobias et al. 2022, <doi:10.1111/ele.13898>), EltonTraits (Wilman et
    al. 2014, <doi:10.1890/13-1917.1>) and the Amniote life-history database
    (Myhrvold et al. 2015, <doi:10.1890/15-0846R.1>).
